# Real offline scans and a synthetic human decision; no model or target execution.
name: Observation gaps preserve the operator's verdict across source revisions
size: 120x36
cwd: @TMP_TARGET
env-unset: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY OPENAI_API_KEY NO_COLOR
env: KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1
shell: python3 @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/observation_gap.py @TMP_TARGET @ART/fixture
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | shell-ready
submit: findings filter state:not_observed
require-live-snap: 30 state:not_observed | gap-queue
expect-not: unknown command
nav-mode:
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 30 ▸ FINDING · | gap-detail
expect: Viewing Review
expect-not: Enter queue → Prove
expect-not: Enter prove
expect: OBSERVATION GAP
expect: gap-base
expect: gap-later
expect: Absence does not establish a fix.
expect: compare scans
ask: Does Review distinguish the confirmation from absence in the later scan, with clear run references?
nav-mode:
keys: Z
resize: 80x24
require-live-snap: 20 ZOOM SELECTED FINDING | gap-detail-80
expect: OBSERVATION GAP
ask: Is the focused detail readable at 80x24, with a visible way to scroll and return?
resize: 60x20
require-live-snap: 20 compare scans | gap-detail-60
ask: Is the selected finding and observation uncertainty understandable at 60x20?
resize: 40x12
require-live-snap: 20 Not seen; no fix established. | gap-detail-40
expect: Not seen; no fix established.
expect: PgUp/PgDn
expect: compare scans
keys: NPage
keys: NPage
keys: NPage
live-snap: gap-detail-40-runs
expect: gap-later
keys: NPage
live-snap: gap-detail-40-scroll
expect: gap-base
expect: Absence does not establish a fix.
ask: Can the operator reach the full observation note at 40x12 without losing navigation?
keys: v
require-live-snap: 30 Sources & context | compare-from-tiny-detail
keys: Escape
require-live-snap: 20 gap-base | return-to-tiny-detail
expect: Absence does not establish a fix.
ask: Does Escape return to the same reading position in the tiny finding detail?
resize: 96x89
keys: g
require-live-snap: 20 F-0001 · confirmed | gap-detail-tall
expect: OBSERVATION GAP
expect-not: before patching
expect-not: decision score
expect-not: legacy triage
ask: Is the tall detail coherent, with the decision and observation note presented as separate facts?
resize: 160x48
require-live-snap: 20 OBSERVATION GAP | gap-detail-wide
expect: OBSERVATION GAP
ask: Does the wide detail use space clearly without stretching short labels into a confusing layout?
keys: v
require-live-snap: 30 Base source: | gap-source-pair
expect: Esc back
expect-not: Esc returns to prompt
ask: Can the operator inspect both source identities and understand which revision each observation belongs to?
keys: Tab
require-live-snap: 30 NOT OBSERVED IN COVERED WORK | gap-comparison
expect: Absence does not establish a fix.
keys: Escape
require-live-snap: 20 OBSERVATION GAP | return-to-wide-detail
expect: compare scans
ask: Does the comparison return to the same finding in its focused detail without switching phases?
keys: C-c
resize: 120x36
env: NO_COLOR=1
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | restarted
paste-file: @ART/fixture/open-command.txt
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 30 describe what to review | restored-gap
expect: OBSERVATION GAP
expect: gap-base
expect: gap-later
ask: After restart without color, does Review preserve both the recorded decision and the observation gap?
keys: C-c
